{"pairs":[{"a":"france/burgundy","b":"united-states/willamette-valley","link":"Pinot Noir, Chardonnay","tag":"","wines":[{"head":"Pinot Noir","text":"Oregon Pinot Noir is often called the closest in style to Burgundy. Burgundy's own leans earthy and floral. The best red Burgundy can be kept for more than 15 years."},{"head":"Chardonnay","text":"Oregon Chardonnay is made around bright acidity rather than a buttery feel. Willamette growers differ on Burgundy: some say their wines are growing more like white Burgundy, while others set out not to copy it."}],"sources":[{"name":"Wine Folly, Pinot Noir","url":"https://winefolly.com/grapes/pinot-noir/"},{"name":"Wikipedia, Burgundy wine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgundy_wine"},{"name":"Oregon Wine Board, Oregon Chardonnay","url":"https://www.oregonwine.org/discover/oregon-chardonnay/"},{"name":"GuildSomm, Neal Hulkower, Willamette Valley's Way with Chardonnay","url":"https://guildsomm.com/public_content/features/articles/b/neal-hulkower/posts/willamette-valley-chardonnay"}]},{"a":"france/bordeaux","b":"united-states/napa-valley","link":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","tag":"","wines":[],"sources":[]},{"a":"france/sancerre","b":"new-zealand/marlborough","link":"Sauvignon Blanc","tag":"","wines":[],"sources":[]},{"a":"spain/rioja","b":"spain/ribera-del-duero","link":"Tempranillo","tag":"","wines":[],"sources":[]},{"a":"italy/barolo","b":"italy/barbaresco","link":"Nebbiolo","tag":"","wines":[],"sources":[]},{"a":"france/champagne","b":"italy/prosecco-doc","link":"Sparkling, made two ways","tag":"different-grapes","wines":[],"sources":[]},{"a":"italy/prosecco-doc","b":"spain/cava","link":"Sparkling, made two ways","tag":"different-grapes","wines":[],"sources":[]},{"a":"france/champagne","b":"spain/cava","link":"Sparkling, both bottle-fermented","tag":"different-grapes","wines":[],"sources":[]},{"a":"france/bordeaux","b":"france/burgundy","link":"France's two great reds","tag":"different-grapes","wines":[],"sources":[